WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.118 --> 00:00:15.192
"There's one!" Raj tried to catch a hopping cricket.

2
00:00:15.193 --> 00:00:17.414
"Oops! I missed it!"

3
00:00:17.415 --> 00:00:20.583
"That's because you used your hands," Parker said.

4
00:00:20.584 --> 00:00:25.177
"I'll get them with my feet!" He lifted a foot to stomp on a cricket.

5
00:00:25.178 --> 00:00:28.740
Daisy grabbed his arm. "No!"

6
00:00:28.741 --> 00:00:32.467
"Hey, you made me miss it!" Parker cried.

7
00:00:32.468 --> 00:00:36.864
"Daisy would never let you hurt an animal," Kaleem said.

8
00:00:36.865 --> 00:00:40.419
"Right," Raj said, staring at Daisy.

9
00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:45.901
"She wanted us to let the crickets out of the tank, and now—"

10
00:00:45.902 --> 00:00:48.686
"They're out of the tank!" Parker said.

11
00:00:48.687 --> 00:00:53.606
He narrowed his eyes. "Did you let them out, Birdbrain?"

12
00:00:53.607 --> 00:00:56.536
Mr. Neal hurried into the classroom.

13
00:00:56.537 --> 00:00:59.755
"I just heard a cricket chirping in the hall."

14
00:00:59.756 --> 00:01:05.430
He gasped when he saw the overturned tank. "Oh no!"

15
00:01:05.431 --> 00:01:09.018
"Daisy let the crickets go," Parker said.

16
00:01:09.019 --> 00:01:13.705
"I did not!" Daisy cried.

17
00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:18.032
"Daisy didn't do it," Grace said shyly.

18
00:01:18.033 --> 00:01:22.536
"She was with me for the entire recess period."

19
00:01:22.537 --> 00:01:25.295
"We can figure out what happened later."

20
00:01:25.296 --> 00:01:29.832
Mr. Neal made shooing motions with his hands.

21
00:01:29.833 --> 00:01:32.121
"Everyone, back outside, please.

22
00:01:32.122 --> 00:01:36.203
I'll ask the janitor to sweep the crickets out of the building."

23
00:01:36.204 --> 00:01:43.477
" Sweep them?" Daisy was

24
00:01:43.478 --> 00:01:46.406
horrified. Mr. Neal

25
00:01:46.407 --> 00:01:49.704
sighed. "I'll ask him to try not to hurt

26
00:01:49.705 --> 00:01:55.302
them. Now go outside,

27
00:01:55.303 --> 00:02:01.991
everyone!" Daisy walked out to the playground with Kaleem and

28
00:02:01.992 --> 00:02:07.497
Grace. "Even if the janitor is careful with the broom, some crickets might be

29
00:02:07.498 --> 00:02:14.466
hurt." Raj overheard her. "So what, Daisy? They're just

30
00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:18.068
bugs." Daisy shook her head, and looked around for

31
00:02:18.069 --> 00:02:22.409
Beatrice. Most people would say that the bumblebee was just a bug too.

32
00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:25.287
But she was Daisy's friend.

33
00:02:25.288 --> 00:02:34.115
Daisy didn't see Beatrice, but she did see a cricket hopping out the door.

34
00:02:34.116 --> 00:02:35.887
"I'll be right back."

35
00:02:35.888 --> 00:02:38.994
She hurried over to the cricket.

36
00:02:38.995 --> 00:02:43.943
"I'm finally free!" he chirped.

37
00:02:43.944 --> 00:02:47.024
Daisy kneeled down to whisper to him.

38
00:02:47.025 --> 00:02:52.973
"I'm glad you're free. But we need to warn your friends about something."

39
00:02:52.974 --> 00:02:57.411
She told the cricket about the janitor with the broom.

40
00:02:57.412 --> 00:03:03.035
"Oh, dear," the cricket said. "I'll see what I can do."

41
00:03:03.036 --> 00:03:08.123
Daisy looked up. Mr. Neal was still inside the building.

42
00:03:08.124 --> 00:03:12.190
So Mrs. Petty, the art teacher, was watching their class.

43
00:03:12.191 --> 00:03:16.041
Luckily, she wasn't looking in Daisy's direction.

44
00:03:16.042 --> 00:03:19.270
Daisy usually obeyed the rules at school.

45
00:03:19.271 --> 00:03:24.074
But this was an emergency.

46
00:03:24.075 --> 00:03:41.494
Moving fast, she sneaked back into the building.

47
00:03:41.495 --> 00:03:46.430
She hurried up and down the hall, looking and listening for crickets.

48
00:03:46.431 --> 00:03:53.235
Every time she found one, she offered to carry it outside.

49
00:03:53.236 --> 00:03:59.949
Soon her pockets were full of crickets.

50
00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:05.149
Finally Mr. Neal spotted her. "What are you doing inside, Daisy?"

51
00:04:05.150 --> 00:04:11.390
"I'm sorry." Daisy hoped the crickets in her pockets wouldn't chirp and give her away.

52
00:04:11.391 --> 00:04:16.259
"I came in to, um, use the bathroom."

53
00:04:16.260 --> 00:04:21.066
She scurried outside before Mr. Neal could respond.

54
00:04:21.067 --> 00:04:25.240
Kaleem was waiting for her. "Did you get all the crickets?"

55
00:04:25.241 --> 00:04:31.777
"I hope so." Daisy helped the crickets out of her pockets.

56
00:04:31.778 --> 00:04:36.077
They hopped away into the bushes, chirping happily.

57
00:04:36.078 --> 00:04:39.283
"We're free! We're free!"

58
00:04:39.284 --> 00:04:42.838
"Thank you, Daisy!" a few crickets said.

59
00:04:42.839 --> 00:04:46.695
Daisy smiled. "You're welcome."

60
00:04:46.696 --> 00:04:50.566
"Uh-oh." Kaleem was staring past her.

61
00:04:50.567 --> 00:04:55.930
"Here comes the janitor!"

